<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold mb-3">Digital Employee Onboarding</h1>
        <p class="lead mb-4">
            Accelerate the velocity of productivity through structured, high-standard transition 
            management for every new joining professional.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Structured Transition Orchestration</h2>
        <p>
            Eliminate onboarding friction with centralized digital checklists that allocate tasks 
            across HR, IT, and Departmental teams. From initial document submission and 
            background verification to the generation of the employment contract from 
            vetted templates, every step is tracked. New joiners can log in to a 
            pre-boarding portal to complete required administrative tasks before their 
            first day, ensuring they enter the office focused on their new role 
            rather than paperwork.
        </p>
        <p>
            Automated creation of user accounts across linked ERP and communication 
            platforms ensures that your new hires are technically equipped to 
            contribute from hour one.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Asset Accountability & Induction</h2>
        <p>
            Protect organizational resources with a digital equipment assignment log. Track 
            the allocation of laptops, mobile devices, access cards, and vehicles 
            directly against the employee record. During the first critical months, 
            the system manages the induction training calendar and schedules 
            probation review milestones, ensuring that every new hire receives the 
            structural support needed to succeed.
        </p>
        <p>
            Induction progress is visualized for managers, highlighting potential areas 
            where additional support or training may be required to bring the employee 
            up to full operational speed.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Probation & Structural Sign-off</h2>
        <p>
            Formalize the end of the transition period with structured probation reviews. 
            Automated notifications alert supervisors to upcoming review dates, providing 
            them with a consolidated view of the employee's induction progress and 
            early performance observations. Final sign-off through the system 
            updates the organizational record from 'Probationary' to 'Permanent,' 
            triggering subsequent benefits eligibility routines within the payroll 
            and HR cores.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

